<title>CANADA: Prairie crops seen safe from frost Sept 15 - CWB.</title>
<headline>Prairie crops seen safe from frost Sept 15 - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most of Canada's Prairie crops should be swathed and safe from the risk of frost if warm overnight temperatures can hold until September 15, a Canadian Wheat Board weather analyst said.</p>
<p>&quot;If we can get as far as September 15, then frost will be a minor issue,&quot; CWB weather and crop surveillance director Paul Bullock told Reuters in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Most spring crops were sown one to two weeks late due to wet and cool weather conditions. Harvest is usually general on the Prairies by the end of August.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
